To create a web page that displays an image with a caption underneath it using HTML and CSS, follow these steps:

1. **Create the HTML structure**: The basic structure of your webpage will include a container for the image and its caption.

2. **Add the image and link**: Place the `<img>` tag inside the `#img-container` div, which is styled to center the image horizontally.

3. **Add the caption**: Use a `<p>` tag within the same `#img-container` div to display the caption.

4. **Make the image clickable**: Add an `href` attribute to the `<a>` tag around the `<img>` tag so that clicking on the image takes users to another website.

Here's how you can implement these steps:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Image with Caption</title>
<style>
  /* Style for the main container */
  #img-container {
    text-align: center;
    padding-top: 50px; /* Optional: Adds some space above the image */
  }

  /* Styling for the image itself */
  #img-container img {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 8px; /* Optional: Adds rounded corners to the image */
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); /* Optional: Adds shadow effect */
  }

  /* Styling for the caption */
  #img-container p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #333;
    line-height: 1.5;
    opacity: 0.7; /* Optional: Makes the caption slightly transparent */
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="img-container">
  <!-- Image -->
  <a href="http://www.example.com">
    <img src="image.jpg" alt="Image">
  </a>

  <!-- Caption -->
  <p>Caption goes here</p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **`<div id="img-container">`**: This creates a container where both the image and the caption will be placed.
- **`<a href="http://www.example.com">`**: This makes the image a hyperlink. When clicked, it redirects to the specified URL (`http://www.example.com`).
- **`<img src="image.jpg" alt="Image">`**: This embeds the image into the webpage. The `alt` attribute provides alternative text for screen readers.
- **`<p>`**: This contains the caption text. It uses `font-size`, `color`, and `line-height` properties to style the text appropriately.

This setup ensures that the image appears centered on the page, has a caption below it, and is linked to another site when clicked. Adjust the styles as needed to fit your design requirements.
